    "note": "Known advisories for the recorded package inventory only. No match is not a security guarantee. Across its commands, Ludion sends package names and versions to OSV (api.osv.dev), and back to OSV the IDs of the advisories it returned; for npm, to the npm registry (registry.npmjs.org); for Composer, to Packagist (packagist.org, repo.packagist.org), and the archive URLs in composer.lock, which name each package's repository and commit, to their hosts (api.github.com, codeload.github.com, github.com, bitbucket.org); for Maven, to Maven Central (repo.maven.apache.org). For PHP Docker it sends the PHP branch to PHP's release list (www.php.net), and for Node.js Docker it downloads Node.js's release index (nodejs.org) whole; for both it sends the image tag (library/php or library/node) to Docker Hub (auth.docker.io, registry-1.docker.io), and Docker pulls the images Ludion builds in from Docker Hub. It downloads CISA's catalog of exploited vulnerabilities (www.cisa.gov) and the EPSS list (epss.empiricalsecurity.com) whole, rather than sending them CVE IDs. `ludion deliver open` pushes each fix's commit to the project's own GitHub repository and opens its PR there; no other source is sent. Major-version fixes, unresolved inventory and unsupported builds require review."
